{title: It Is Well with My Soul}
{artist: Horatio G. Spafford (1828-1888)}
{key: C}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
When [C]peace like a river at[F]tendeth my [C]way,
When [Am]sorrows like [D]sea billows [G]roll;
What[C]ever my lot, Thou hast [F]taught me to [Dm]say,
It is [C]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eov}

{soc}
It is [C]well [G]with my [C]soul,
It is [F]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 2}
Though [C]Satan should buffet, though [F]trials should [C]come,
Let [Am]this blest as[D]surance con[G]trol,
That [C]Christ hath regarded my [F]helpless es[Dm]tate,
And hath [C]shed His own [G]blood for my [C]soul.
{eov}

{soc}
It is [C]well [G]with my [C]soul,
It is [F]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 3}
My [C]sin, O the bliss of this [F]glorious [C]thought,
My [Am]sin, not in [D]part but the [G]whole,
Is [C]nailed to the cross, and I [F]bear it no [Dm]more,
Praise the [C]Lord, praise the [G]Lord, O my [C]soul!
{eov}

{soc}
It is [C]well [G]with my [C]soul,
It is [F]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eoc}

{sov: Verse 4}
And [C]Lord, haste the day when my [F]faith shall be [C]sight,
The [Am]clouds be rolled [D]back as a [G]scroll;
The [C]trump shall resound, and the [F]Lord shall de[Dm]scend,
Even [C]so, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eov}

{soc}
It is [C]well [G]with my [C]soul,
It is [F]well, it is [G]well with my [C]soul.
{eoc}
